# The web server, which everything else about nginx waits on.
#
# One of three files -- `examples/resources/unit/nginx` and
# `examples/templates/etc/nginx/conf.d/60-detc.conf` are the others -- that
# together are the worked example of `_requires`.  Read the header of the unit,
# which is where the argument is.
#
# Nothing is declared but the package.  `installed: true` is the default of the
# schema and is written out because a file that only said `{}` would read like
# a mistake.
#
# There is no `_order`: the `pkg` provider declares 10, which is before the
# templates at 50 and before the unit at 70, and that is exactly the order this
# example needs.  A declaration that repeats an order it agrees with is one more
# thing to keep in step with the provider.
#
# The name is the name the distribution uses.  It is `nginx` on openSUSE,
# Debian and Fedora alike, which is why this example uses it and not something
# that has to be chosen by reading `system.pkg.manager`.
installed: true
